# Project Instructions

Follow these guidelines when building LLaMAlert (see README.md).

## General
- Always write complete, production-ready code; no placeholders or stubs.
- Enforce strict typing, clear error handling and consistent formatting.
- Include docstrings, comments and adhere to style guides for each language.
- Never commit secrets; use environment variables.

## Frontend (React + TypeScript)
- Use function components + React.memo and custom hooks (`useX`).
- Enable TS strict mode, explicit `Props` interfaces, avoid `any`.
- Build forms for typing biometrics and geolocation; show real-time confidence bars (0–100%), green for legit, red for anomalies.
- Apply minimalist, professional styling; follow accessible color and spacing standards.
- Test with Jest + React Testing Library; cover UI, hooks and edge states.

## Backend (Python + FastAPI)
- Use async FastAPI (`async def`) with Pydantic models for request/response.
- Expose `/infer` endpoint for anomaly detection; optional CRUD for synthetic data.
- Adhere to PEP 8, include type hints and comprehensive docstrings.
- Integrate OpenTelemetry spans around inference and DB operations.
- Return structured JSON errors with HTTP status codes.

## Database (PostgreSQL)
- Schema: typing metrics, geolocation, inference logs with `created_at`/`updated_at`.
- Manage schema via Alembic migrations; enforce constraints and indexes on heavy queries.
- Use async driver or SQLAlchemy ORM; pool connections efficiently.

## LLM Integration
- Load and cache LLaMA-2-7B from Hugging Face; target <2 s per request.
- Craft clear prompts for typing-pattern and location anomalies.
- Gracefully handle model/IO errors and fallbacks.

## Deployment (Vercel)
- Deploy frontend and FastAPI backend as serverless functions.
- Configure `vercel.json` for build/dev commands; manage env vars in dashboard.
- Monitor performance and logs via Vercel analytics.

## Testing & CI
- Frontend: Jest + React Testing Library.
- Backend: pytest with coverage; test business logic, endpoints, error paths.
- CI: lint, type-check and run all tests on every push.
